{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 40","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d81f7ac03ef836f5de9465aa8366e8051de7c3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq x\\leq 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb6f45528909ced3202717ade02d50d0a30fa3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x^2\\}=\\{x\\}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"19\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f845944fd516023c47bdd58ede2ae71a946b10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor S\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace36a85b5a60841555a6f3b85d74855dc367641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor + \\{ x \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />.  That results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d6a9d084b033dbd60014535ae6b077a7fc1d05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\{ 2 \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\{ x \\} + \\{ x \\}^2 \\} = \\{ x \\}^2\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" />\nNote that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f55a664bec43f164cb6dc0fa3b37e6e4ea2db04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\{ x \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" /> is not an integer, than both sides can not equal each other.  Thus, to find all solutions where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1e141537d099ad734eb9858e36f1d1cc8159911.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le x \\le 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, find the values where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f55a664bec43f164cb6dc0fa3b37e6e4ea2db04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\{ x \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" /> is an integer.\n</p>\n<ul><li>The easier case is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37e4e00370bd693ebd11cc63145b02fdac5cea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ x \\} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, so both sides equal each other.  Therefore, every integer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a solution.</li>\n<li>The harder case is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/87393e6d77e4f48595c0819394f45983e724c175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = n \\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73119f04d6ae5f6eb4afc8c9c946a5744a11be50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> integers, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/9611a10934d20932453450ad8990985b21a1363e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />.  That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/5045dfb24b263d88fd23de92a2867c738e077738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\lfloor x \\rfloor \\{ x \\} = 2n \\cdot \\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"33\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.  That means every mixed number in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890a4e198dec7482bb8229172be11b9e86b1bb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\frac{c}{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca20323097849872f269fe638886da88c852fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; c &lt; 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> works.</li></ul>\n<p>With that taken in consideration, the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de1912cb0399e0607bc0e0f9ac2e72198807380.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1 + 1\\frac{1}{2}) + (2 + 2\\frac{1}{4} \\cdots) \\cdots (98 + 98\\frac{1}{196} \\cdots) + 99\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"37\" />\nThe arithmetic series sum formula can be used to simplify things further.  If the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88de9ca9e57c01429547cc8c45082db849f52386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />, and last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff9d61ce388666c505153a30795c08acea4ef7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - \\frac{1}{2n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />, the sum of the terms in the series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba94a1bc451659837185ba4589bd00cf671ccbed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2n(2n+1 - \\frac{1}{2n})}{2} = 2n^2 + n - \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"249\" height=\"40\" />.  Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/0153afa9ca3f907cf9434f84878bef1950d3a941.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{98} (2n^2 + n - \\frac{1}{2} ) + 99\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"50\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/088c0806ee78844072540f2b897c646e5e557fd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\sum_{n=1}^{98} (n^2) + \\sum_{n=1}^{98} (n) - 98 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 99\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"50\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab49b59c05d72d41e0c7b71d245b343edfd26a2d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 \\cdot \\frac{98 \\cdot 99 \\cdot 197}{6} + \\frac{99 \\cdot 98}{2} - 49 + 99\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e6eb769c9d02c148f096fabbe2d216bbb7df47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[49 \\cdot 33 \\cdot 397 + 50\\]\" width=\"129\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/eadc2fb54ac47448dd0ddaf19e428ce4af9bb976.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[641999\\]\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/52616b2bd53545b23609107fb16f6202097e3ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor S \\rfloor = \\boxed{641999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_40&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 39\">Problem 39</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_41\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 41\">Problem 41</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.